+H2 comp. The Q3 guide [S87] is about +1% and already embeds the roughly 200bp late-July cyclospora softness. Near-term guides have come in at or better than guided 11 of 11 times (Q1 beat by about 2 points, Q2 by 1.2), so I take Q3 at about 1.8%. Q4 laps a -2.5% compare, and pricing steps from 1.6% (Q2) to mid-2% (Q3) to matching inflation from Q4 [S80, S89]. That puts Q4 near 2.6% and H2 near 2.2%. On H1 comps of 0.5 and 2.2, this gives FY2026 of about 1.8%, inside the 1 to 3 guide [G47] and just under its 2.08 bias-adjusted mid. I hold it below the default 2.82 because the two-year stack is still negative (Q2 about -1.8) and the 'softer in recent weeks' comment is a statement against interest [S78]. H2 units. H1 printed 6.9 and 7.1pp, H2 2025 was 7.2 and 7.4pp, and openings are guided 350 to 370 versus 345 [G48], with management 3 of 3 at or above midpoint. That supports 7.1pp, but Middle East partner delays [S61] keep it flat rather than higher. Persistence. H1 ratios deteriorated about 2.6pp in total (food +0.59, labor +0.49, other +1.02, occupancy +0.23). H2 2025 already absorbed much of the cause. Margin fell 100bp in Q3 2025 and 140bp in Q4 2025 once pricing started lagging mid-single-digit inflation [S14, S15]. Marketing stepped up 90bp and 50bp in those quarters [S16, S48]. Food ratios ran 30.0 and 30.2 versus about 29 in H1 2025. So H2 2026 laps the start of the dislocation, while price rises toward inflation. Against that, Q4 2025 contained a one-off 70bp gift-card benefit [S43] that may not recur, and hospitality labor reinvestment continues [S37, S81]. Taking those together, half of the H1 deterioration persists (0.5). Versus consensus: the default bridge gave $1.067. Lowering persistence to 0.5 adds about $0.05 and the lower comp takes back about $0.01, which lands FY2026 near $1.11 to $1.12. That is roughly 3% below consensus $1.15 and implies H2 EPS of about $0.55 versus $0.54 in H2 2025. Consensus needs about $0.58, which requires a sharper margin inflection than the gift-card lap and the reinvestment statements support.
 
