+### A7. Driver notes by case
+**Bull:** traffic_pct: Q2 transactions were +1.0% with digital mix up 280bp. Bull extends this to +2% as HEEP capacity and the lapping of the -2.5% Q4 2025 base help. It depends on the open promises S12 and S21. check_pct: Price runs about 3.3%, matching inflation [S89], with CPI food away from home at +3.7% providing headroom. Mix is about -0.1 as extra-protein incidence holds [S38]. unit_contribution_pp: Openings run modestly above guide, consistent with management landing at or above midpoint 3 of 3 times. New-store productivity holds. food_inflation_pct: Processed poultry PPI is -12.5% and processed foods +0.1%, which offsets beef (+3.1% PPI). Supplier savings [S30] are not relied on. wage_inflation_pct: Leisure and hospitality earnings are +3.9% YoY. Bull assumes slight cooling. labor_efficiency_pct: Assumes part of the 2 to 3 HEEP hours is kept rather than reinvested. This contradicts the current stance [S37] and depends on the untested S07 promise. occupancy_inflation_pct: Lessors PPI is +3.5%. Close to that across cases. other_inflation_pct: Near CPI +3.7%, with marketing held flat as a share of sales after the 2025 step-up. g_and_a_growth_pct: G&A grows well below revenue as Recipe for Growth costs annualize. This relies on S82 (category e), so it is a bull-only assumption. share_reduction_pct: Buybacks continue near $2B or more at a low price. The money-backed record [S17, S49, S68, S83] supports capacity. tax_rate_pct: Matches the 23.7% bias-adjusted figure from a 0 of 3 above-midpoint record [G49].
+**Base:** traffic_pct: Q1 +0.6 and Q2 +1.0 transactions, but the Q3 guide implies traffic plus mix near -1.5. Base takes about the 2026 average, held back by the LTO lap. check_pct: Price about 3.0%, matching inflation from Q4 2026 [S89, formal guidance]. Mix about -0.2, improving from -1.0 (Q1) and -0.4 (Q2). unit_contribution_pp: This has run 6.9 to 7.4pp for six quarters. Similar openings on a larger base hold it near 7.0. food_inflation_pct: The FY2026 guide is 4% [G40]. For 2027, poultry deflation (PPI -12.5%) and flat processed foods (+0.1%) offset beef (+3.1% PPI, retail +10.7%). This sits just under check, so the food ratio is roughly flat. wage_inflation_pct: Leisure and hospitality average hourly earnings +3.9% YoY. labor_efficiency_pct: Small. Management says HEEP hours are reinvested [S37, statement against interest] and labor execution is being deliberately raised [S81]. occupancy_inflation_pct: Lessors of nonresidential buildings PPI +3.5%. other_inflation_pct: Slightly under CPI +3.7%, since the marketing step-up is already in the base. g_and_a_growth_pct: H1 2026 G&A grew 16.6% on Recipe for Growth costs. That eases as it annualizes but stays near revenue growth because catering launches in 2027 and remodel spend continues. Some leverage, not the leverage S82 promises. share_reduction_pct: Average count falls about 4.3% if buybacks run near $1.6B to $2B a year at low-$30s prices. The cash constraint is analyst inference, not reported, so I do not cut further. tax_rate_pct: The Q2 adjusted rate was 24.0%. Actuals have run 1.8 to 2.4pp under guide midpoints.
+**Bear:** traffic_pct: The Q3 guide implies traffic plus mix of about -1.5 under cyclospora. Bear holds that through 2027 as LTOs are lapped and the competitive set (CAVA, Sweetgreen) takes share. check_pct: Price around 2.5% because management keeps protecting value, as in 2025 and 2026 [S15, S58]. Mix stays negative at about -0.3. unit_contribution_pp: Weaker new-unit productivity. The 80% productivity and 60% return metrics stopped being disclosed [M01, M02], and Middle East delays continue. food_inflation_pct: Retail ground beef +10.7% and tariffs keep inputs in the mid single digits, as the CFO warned [S14]. Poultry deflation reverses. wage_inflation_pct: Slightly above the +3.9% leisure and hospitality print. labor_efficiency_pct: Hospitality labor investment [S81] and turnover push hours up. HEEP savings are fully reinvested. occupancy_inflation_pct: Slightly above lessors PPI +3.5%. Small spread across cases. other_inflation_pct: Above CPI +3.7% as marketing rises again to defend traffic and catering launch costs land. g_and_a_growth_pct: Close to the 10.2% Q2 G&A growth, plus recurring restructuring and catering costs. share_reduction_pct: Buybacks slow toward about $1.5B if cash is depleted, as the falling interest income suggests. Share-based compensation offsets part. tax_rate_pct: Toward the 25% guide midpoint, with less share-based compensation benefit at low prices.
